# Allowlist for .github/claims/attachment-claims.py (run it for the rules).
#
# Every line that says attachment contents are unavailable, that attachments
# are never (or not) opened, downloaded or read, or that attachment bytes or
# file contents are out of reach (in English, Portuguese, Spanish, French or
# German) must be here,
# under the connections a reviewer checked it is true for:
#   metadata    the hosted metadata connector (api.…/mcp, self-hosted
#               containers), 'metadata' connections, the local reader
#               without plaintext
#   text        text connections of the attested reader (consent version 1,
#               or 2 without attachments) and the local reader with plaintext
#   media       media connections: what they still never open (view-once,
#               gone, keyless or unhashed media, audio and voice notes)
#   unrelated   about something else entirely
# A sentence true of several names them all, joined by ','. A general claim
# that Wappie's connector never opens attachments is not allowed: since A1
# the attested reader at mcp.…/mcp does, for media connections.
#
#   <scope> <path>                 every hit in the file (code; give the reason)
#   <scope> <path> :: <fragment>   only hits whose line contains the fragment

